<!--
================================================================================
  putPatientProblemList (VISIT DIAGNOSIS variant) — Sample XML
  Project:    NEHR Onboarding — Heart Clinic / MDXcess GCMS
  Spec ref:   putPatientProblemList_v0.2_(VD)_20251224.xlsx (Synapxe), Request tab
  Generated:  2026-07-08
  SUPERSEDES: the May PPL deliverables (NEHR_putPatientProblemList_Sample_Full /
              _Sample_Mandatory / _Reference_AllFieldsFilled, PPL walkthrough,
              PPL_Developer_Reference.xlsx). Decision 2026-07-08: contribute
              VISIT DIAGNOSIS, not PPL (NEHR 07-Jul: VD is the outpatient norm).

  SCENARIO
  =================
  Mr TAN AH BENG (71 y/o male, NRIC S5512345A) — same continuity patient as the
  medication / allergy / referral samples. His 2026-07-07 consultation with
  Dr Ruth Kam (the visit that also produced the referral sample): two chronic
  active diagnoses reviewed and coded — Paroxysmal AF and Essential HTN.

  VISIT-DIAGNOSIS RULES (vs the old PPL model)
  =================
  1. SAME web service + reconciliation filenames as PPL — only the payload
     semantics change. listType is the switch:
        listType = "Visit Diagnosis List"   (LITERAL, CASE-SENSITIVE)
  2. recordIdentifier is assigned PER VISIT — a fresh list every visit, never
     reused across visits. (PPL would have required one longitudinal list.)
     [GCMS] propose: <Appointment_ID>-VD
  3. eventId MUST equal the putEvent id for the same visit ([GCMS]
     Tbl_PatientAppointment.Appointment_ID).
  4. VD is MANDATORY for every actualised outpatient visit with >=1 diagnosis;
     all diagnoses of the same visit go in ONE message payload.
  5. Non-diagnostic visit (e.g. report collection): still send, with an
     administrative diagnosis carrying the non-diagnostic SNOMED-CT code —
     ask SPOC for the exact concept code Synapxe expects.
  6. Diagnosis coding = SNOMED CT (SG Extension); codingSchemeVersion carries
     the SNOMED release agreed with the standards team (e.g. "Jul2024").
     SNOMED codes below are indicative — [VERIFY] against the SG Extension
     release GCMS adopts before SIT.
  7. Amendment/cancellation: resend with the SAME recordIdentifier and
     problem ids; listStatus/reasonForCancellation signal cancellation.
================================================================================
-->
